meta {
  name: Option Snapshot
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

get {
  url: {{webullBaseUrl}}/openapi/market-data/option/snapshot?symbols=SPY271217P00500000&category=US_OPTION
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  symbols: SPY271217P00500000
  category: US_OPTION
}

docs {
  The current quote for one option contract, named by its OCC symbol in the
  `symbols` query parameter, edited on the Params tab (root, yymmdd, C or P, strike x 1000 in eight digits, for
  example `SPY271217P00500000`).

  No assertion on purpose: until US options market data is enabled for these API keys,
  Webull answers

  ```
  403 {"error_code":"MARKET_DATA_NOT_SUBSCRIBED",
       "message":"Insufficient permission, please subscribe to US_OPTION."}
  ```

  A 200 here is the sign that the subscription is active. The backend does not call
  this endpoint yet; open option positions are unpriced for that reason.

  There is also `/openapi/market-data/option/bars` for a contract's history. It exists
  (it answers 400 rather than 404), but its parameters are not confirmed, so it has no
  request here yet.
}
